– HARD RULES

The goal is to abandon Gradio for the WebUI frontend and instead repurpose the original Forge (WebUI) API to serve a new ViteUI frontend.

Build the UI entirely with React and Vite (located in: /client/src/)

This is a hybrid project:
Original Forge code is kept only to:
- Pull upstream improvements
- Maintain compatibility with extensions
- Support future Forge/WebUI changes

The untouched reference copy of Forge lives in:
original-forge/ (READ-ONLY)
This folder is FOR REFERENCE ONLY.

🚫 NEVER modify, run, or depend on the following files or paths:
launch.py
launch_utils.py
webui*.bat
webui*.py
webui*.sh
viteui does not use these files at runtime.

ViteUI Fork:
Modifying Forge Code (LAST RESORT)
Only if absolutely unavoidable, you may touch code inside:
/modules/, /modules_forge/, /extensions-builtin/, /extensions/, /backend/, /scripts/
When this happens:
Changes must be minimal and new business logic must be handled externally in modules_viteapi/ using wrappers, adapters, shims, etc.

Client Testing:
To test client-side changes without conflicts, always run:
cd client
npm run build

NEVER RUN npm run dev